{
  "tema": 6960,
  "slug": "empezar-a-infinitivo",
  "titulo": "Empezar / comenzar a + infinitive: to start doing something",
  "subtitulo": "Empecé a surfear, comenzaron a construir: always a + infinitive.",
  "foto": "t07.jpg",
  "regla": "Empezar / comenzar (conjugated) + a + infinitive = to start doing. Always the a, always an infinitive, never a gerund.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-10",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "To say _to start doing_ something, use **empezar** or **comenzar** (conjugated) + **a** + **infinitive**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "formula",
          "partes": [
            "**empezar / comenzar**",
            "**a**",
            "infinitive"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "The **a** always follows. After it comes an **infinitive**, never a gerund: English says _start working_, Spanish says **empieza a trabajar**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Both verbs are **e > ie** in the present (**empiezo**, **comienzo**) and change **z > c** before **e** (**empecé**, **empiece**)."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "A similar structure: **ponerse a** + infinitive, _to set about doing_: **me puse a estudiar**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: **a** is the starting line; behind it, the plain infinitive."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "Esta semana ==empecé a bailar== salsa.",
              "en": "This week I started dancing salsa."
            },
            {
              "es": "Beto ==comienza a gritar== cuando no lo escuchas.",
              "en": "Beto starts shouting when you don't listen to him."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Empezaremos a estudiar== alemán la próxima semana.",
              "en": "We'll start studying German next week."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Comenzaron a construir== las casas ayer.",
              "en": "They started building the houses yesterday."
            },
            {
              "es": "Ustedes ==han empezado a resolver== sus problemas solos.",
              "en": "You've started solving your problems on your own."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Empezó a llover== justo cuando salimos.",
              "en": "It started raining just as we left."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
